59
00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:33.040
Your turn. Say: Discipline.

60
00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:36.924
Discipline.

61
00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.010
Ownership of learning.

62
00:03:40.017 --> 00:03:44.187
Ownership of learning means taking responsibility for your own progress.

63
00:03:44.783 --> 00:03:47.700
Ownership of learning makes students stronger.

64
00:03:48.317 --> 00:03:51.480
Your turn. Say: Ownership of learning.

65
00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:55.985
Ownership of learning.

66
00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.729
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:04:01.583 --> 00:04:03.734
Visal, how do you study on your own?

68
00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:11.844
I plan my week. The development of self-discipline supports independent learning.

69
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.741
What keeps you motivated?

70
00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:20.360
My curiosity. The discovery of new ideas makes me happy.

71
00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.799
Any advice?

72
00:04:23.883 --> 00:04:28.103
Yes. The regular review of your goals helps you stay on track.

73
00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:30.895
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.051
Grammar focus: Nominalization.

75
00:04:34.351 --> 00:04:35.480
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:36.183 --> 00:04:40.110
The development of self-discipline supports independent learning.

77
00:04:41.017 --> 00:04:43.423
The discovery of new ideas motivates me.

78
00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.827
The review of my goals keeps me focused.

79
00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:56.456
Nominalization turns a verb into a noun: develop → development, discover → discovery. It makes writing sound more academic.

80
00:04:57.217 --> 00:05:01.251
Be careful! Don't say: The develop of discipline helps learning.

81
00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.152
Say: The development of discipline helps learning.

82
00:05:06.452 --> 00:05:09.717
Use the noun form: develop → development.

83
00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.187
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.396
Learning on My Own.

85
00:05:15.696 --> 00:05:18.520
Independent learning means taking ownership of learning.

86
00:05:19.533 --> 00:05:22.090
The development of self-discipline supports it.

87
00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.493
Intrinsic motivation and curiosity keep learners going.

88
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.649
Metacognition helps them understand how they learn best.

89
00:05:31.633 --> 00:05:34.864
Lifelong learning starts with self-directed study today.

90
00:05:35.967 --> 00:05:39.980
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:40.817 --> 00:05:43.501
The development blank self-discipline helps.

92
00:05:43.801 --> 00:05:46.421
A, of. B, for. C, in.

93
00:05:49.967 --> 00:05:51.432
The answer is A: of.

94
00:05:52.583 --> 00:05:54.513
Thinking about how you learn is blank.

95
00:05:54.813 --> 00:05:58.699
A, metacognition. B, discipline. C, autonomy.

96
00:06:02.233 --> 00:06:04.233
The answer is A: metacognition.

97
00:06:05.383 --> 00:06:09.194
Wanting to learn because you enjoy it is blank motivation.

98
00:06:09.494 --> 00:06:13.066
A, intrinsic. B, external. C, lifelong.

99
00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.576
The answer is A: intrinsic.

100
00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:22.732
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:26.036
How do you stay motivated to learn on your own?

102
00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:36.443
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:36.743 --> 00:06:46.141
I stay motivated by setting small goals. The completion of each goal gives me energy, and I reward myself every weekend.

104
00:06:46.441 --> 00:06:48.313
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:49.217 --> 00:06:53.239
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and nominalization.

106
00:06:53.539 --> 00:06:58.746
Today's value is self-discipline. Control your habits, so your habits do not control you.

107
00:06:59.046 --> 00:07:01.466
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

108
00:07:01.766 --> 00:07:04.511
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

